<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc238560355" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 18: Table between numbered list in a workflow</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an alarm escalation workflow where a table provides reference information between workflow stages.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>workflow</keyword>
        <keyword>between</keyword>
        <keyword>table</keyword>
        <keyword>Alarm</keyword>
        <keyword>Table</keyword>
        <keyword>numbered</keyword>
        <indexterm>workflow</indexterm>
        <indexterm>between</indexterm>
        <indexterm>table</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section><p>Consider an alarm escalation workflow where a table provides reference information between workflow stages.</p>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Table between a numbered list (workflow)</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry> .md input </entry>
                     <entry> DITA output </entry>
                  </row>                  
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock># Alarm Escalation Workflow
  1. Alarm Detection
  | Severity | Response Time |
  |-----------|-----------|
  | Critical | Immediate |
  | Warning | 15 Minutes |
  2. Notification Delivery
  3. Resolution</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>&lt;concept id="alarm_escalation_workflow"&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Alarm Escalation Workflow&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;conbody&gt;
  &lt;ol&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Alarm Detection
  &lt;simpletable&gt;
  &lt;sthead&gt;
  &lt;stentry&gt;Severity&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;stentry&gt;Response Time&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;/sthead&gt;
  &lt;strow&gt;
  &lt;stentry&gt;Critical&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;stentry&gt;Immediate&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;/strow&gt;
  &lt;strow&gt;     &lt;stentry&gt;Warning&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;stentry&gt;15 Minutes&lt;/stentry&gt;
  &lt;/strow&gt;
  &lt;/simpletable&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Notification Delivery&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Resolution&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
  &lt;/conbody&gt;
  &lt;/concept&gt;</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter preserves both the workflow list and the table. Because the table is in the context of the first list item, the table is positioned inside that <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> tag.</p></section></refbody>
</reference>
